{"kind": "local_or_unclassified_prose", "line": 9518, "review_required": true, "scope_stack": [], "text_excerpt": "Suppose $\\mathfrak p$, $\\mathfrak p'$ are primes of the ring $R$. Let $X = \\Spec(R)$ with the Zariski topology. Denote $x \\in X$ the point corresponding to $\\mathfrak p$ and $x' \\in X$ the point corresponding to $\\mathfrak p'$. Then we have: $$ x' \\leadsto x \\Leftrightarrow \\mathfrak p' \\subset \\mathfrak p. $$ In words: $x$ is a specialization of $x'$ if and only if $\\mathfrak p' \\subset \\mathfrak p$. See Topology, Section \\ref{topology-section-specialization} for terminology and notation."}
